    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d670">

                <pb facs="0705" n="693" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg693"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">868.248/130</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Telephone Conversation, by the Chief of
                        the Division of Near Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1941-02-15">February 15, 1941</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Greek Minister telephoned me this morning to say that he had just come from
                    Secretary Knox’s office where he was informed that his Government would receive
                    during the course of next month thirty <hi rendition="#italic">new</hi> Grumman
                    planes and that fifteen of the old Grumman planes previously under discussion
                    would be available to his Government if it desired them. Admiral Towers was
                    present with Secretary Knox when this information was conveyed to the Greek
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>The Minister was in a state of great excitement and exhilaration over this
                    development and repeatedly expressed his appreciation to officials of the
                    Department for assisting him in arriving at this final and highly satisfactory
                    solution of the problem of furnishing planes to Greece.</p>
                <p>The Minister said he desired to call at the Department on Monday to express his
                    further appreciation.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
